{"message":"$450 on an average balance of about $96,000 is roughly equivalent to a 5.625% annualized rate if the balance stayed constant for a full month, so it may be close to the Gold account’s base rate rather than unusually low. Interest is calculated daily and credited monthly, so the exact amount depends on your daily balances and the number of days in the statement period.

Your Gold account may also qualify for additional APY from eligible checking-account pairings and the highest applicable credit-card bonus. These bonuses do not all stack within their category: only the highest checking boost and highest credit-card bonus apply, though they can combine with other bonuses.

I can review your actual account, interest transaction, checking accounts, and credit cards to confirm whether you’re receiving the best applicable rate. Before I access your information, please provide any two of these identity details: date of birth, email address, phone number, or mailing address."}

